            "text": "A JWT is decoded without verifying its signature, then its claims are trusted. Anyone can forge `{\"sub\":\"1\",\"role\":\"admin\"}` in base64 — full account takeover. Fix: Use jwt.verify(token, secret, { algorithms: [\"HS256\"] }) (or the framework session helper) and only trust verified claims."
